Z||000000||wjluciano||03-15-2001||02:28 PM||||Does any one know of a good priced kit that can be purchased for a 1986 fiero se. Ive seen the Countach kits but thats it. also any tips to pull the most power out of a stock fiero v6<P>------------------<BR>Warren Luciano<BR>wjluciano@hotmail.com||||reg||5
Z||000001||Mr.Frosty||03-15-2001||02:36 PM||||Look into the Ferrari 355 kit.It is about $6500.00 and it is the best looking kit I <BR>think anyway.At least in the lines and shape.<BR>It requires a slight strectch to the wheelbase though.kitcars.com has links and info I think,and some for sale too.Look for the dark orient blue one and you'll see what I mean.<P>------------------<BR>88 Formula T-top <BR>85 GT Turbo||||reg||6
Z||000002||Jay||03-15-2001||06:34 PM||||Yes the 355 Kit is the best one yet.  However, beware.  My friend who is a body man and has lots of experience in kits spent about a year modifying the body to be straight.  The hoods are warped and the front bumper is uneven on one side.  Rear bumper also needs alot of attention.  They look great if you do them right.  If you think you can put it together in the 50 hours they claim, think again!  It is alot of work!!  And Ferrari goes after suppliers of 355 kits big time!!! Make sure you get everything up front, they may not be around a few months later.  But the 355 is probably the best looking Ferrari kit ever produced, if you spend the bucks and time to do it right.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||03-15-2001||07:18 PM||||there is a nice looking Ford GT 40 that fits a stock wb Fiero, I didnt want to do any cutting in mine. Its a 308 GTB, but dont think anyone makes them anymore. Check ebay, there is always kits in there for $2000-$3000 unfinished. Some guy on forum was taking a finished frame with a TestaRossa to Carlisle for $2500.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||mshill||03-15-2001||10:35 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.bodykitz.com" TARGET=_blank>www.bodykitz.com</A> <P>Don't expect anything from these guys to be "bolt-on".  I am currently putting together the F-50 kit.  It is a lot of work to get it all straight.<P>||||reg||1
